%N A402128 Number of plane partitions of n whose row sums and column sums are all pairwise distinct.
%C A402128 All nonzero row sums and column sums, taken together, must be pairwise distinct. In particular, no row sum may equal any column sum.
%C A402128 Equivalently, a(n) counts nonnegative integer matrices with entries summing to n, without zero rows or columns, whose rows are pairwise comparable under componentwise order, whose columns are likewise pairwise comparable, and whose row and column sums are all pairwise distinct. Matrices are counted up to independent permutations of rows and columns.
%e A402128 The matrix [[7,5,3],[4,3,1],[2,1,1]] is counted by a(27): its rows satisfy (7,5,3) >= (4,3,1) >= (2,1,1) componentwise, and its columns satisfy (7,4,2) >= (5,3,1) >= (3,1,1) componentwise. Its row sums are 15,8,4 and its column sums are 13,9,5, all pairwise distinct.
%Y A402128 Cf. A000219, A319646, A306320.
